# Terraform local state and sensitive variable files
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
# scripts/deploy-router-image.sh stages its rewrite in a mode-600 temp file
# beside dev.tfvars. `*.tfvars` above does not match a name with a suffix after
# `.tfvars`, and BSD mktemp only substitutes a TRAILING run of X's, so the temp
# name cannot both be unique and end in `.tfvars`. Ignore the prefix instead:
# a SIGKILL mid-rewrite leaves behind the client secret and both OAuth tokens.
*.tfvars.tmp.*
# Saved plan files. A plan embeds sensitive values in PLAINTEXT regardless of
# `sensitive = true` — that only redacts CLI output — so a committed plan leaks
# the Linear client secret and both OAuth tokens exactly as state would. Bare
# `tfplan` alone is too narrow: `-out=` takes any name, and `tfplan.bin` /
# `plan.out` are common enough that one of them will get used.
tfplan*
*.tfplan
plan.out

# Claude worktrees
.claude/worktrees
.superpowers/
